        "nb" : {
          "@type" : "RESOURCE_DESCRIPTION_ITEM",
          "language" : {
            "terminologyId" : {
              "value" : "ISO_639-1"
            },
            "codeString" : "nb"
          },
          "purpose" : "For å støtte registreringen av en oversikt eller oppsummering av en bekreftet graviditet og utfall, inkludert svangerskapsperioden, fødselen og den umiddelbare postpartum perioden.",
          "keywords" : [ "graviditet", "svangerskap", "foster", "spedbarn", "neonatal", "forløsning", "befruktning", "termin", "termindato", "forventet", "fødsel", "baby", "babyer" ],
          "use" : "*Use to record an overview or summary record of an identified pregnancy and outcome, including the antenatal period, labor, birth and the immediate postnatal period. \r\n\r\nDuring an active pregnancy, this archetype supports the evolution of a persistent pregnancy-related health summary record, with information gradually accumulated or updated, throughout the duration of the pregnancy, labour, birth and the immediate postnatal period. As the data is committed to the persistent health record, the date of the update is also recorded in the 'Last Updated' data element in Protocol, to ensure that if this pregnancy summary is taken out of context of the health record for other purposes, such as data exchange, the date of the latest update is kept with the clinical data.\r\n\r\nAfter birth, this summary record can be used to share essential information with other healthcare providers about the pregnancy, labour, birth and immediate postnatal period. \r\n\r\nEach completed pregnancy summary saved to the health record can be re-used to populate the Past Pregnancy History details in subsequent pregnancy records.\r\n\r\nIn situations where completed pregnancy summaries are not available for each previous pregnancy, this archetype can also be used to record a relevant subset of information that can be used to populate the Past Pregnancy History details with new or active pregnancy records. (en)",
          "misuse" : "Brukes ikke for å dokumentere event-based informasjon i løpet av graviditeten, fødsel og den umiddelbare postpartum perioden. Disse vil bli dokumentert ved bruk av OBSERVATION arketyper, for eksempel informasjon som er relatert til historikk og undersøkelser ved svangerskapskontroller og under fødselen.\r\n\r\nBrukes ikke for å dokumentere sammenfattet informasjon om kvinnens obstetriske historie - bruk EVALUATION.obstetric_summary.\r\n\r\nBrukes ikke for å dokumentere detaljert informasjon om kvinnens menstruasjonssyklus - bruk OBSERVATION.menstrual_cycle.\r\n\r\nBrukes ikke for å dokumentere detaljert informasjon om spedbarns måltider/mating - en seperat arketype vil bli brukt til dette formålet.\r\n\r\nBrukes ikke for å dokumentere en generell sammenfattet menstruasjonshistorikk eller menstruasjonsdagbok - seperate arketyper vil bli brukt til dette formålet.",
          "copyright" : "© openEHR Foundation",
          "originalResourceUri" : { },
          "otherDetails" : { }
        },
        "pt-br" : {
          "@type" : "RESOURCE_DESCRIPTION_ITEM",
          "language" : {
            "terminologyId" : {
              "value" : "ISO_639-1"
            },
            "codeString" : "pt-br"
          },
          "purpose" : "*To support the recording of an overview or summary record of an identified pregnancy and outcome, including the antenatal period, labor, birth and the immediate postnatal period. (en)",
          "keywords" : [ "gravidez", "feto", "feto", "infantil", "neonato", "parto", "concepção", "aguardado", "data", "esperado", "trabalho de parto", "parto", "nascimento", "bebê", "bebês", "data provável do parto", "data prevista do nascimento" ],
          "use" : "*Use to record an overview or summary record of an identified pregnancy and outcome, including the antenatal period, labor, birth and the immediate postnatal period. \r\n\r\nDuring an active pregnancy, this archetype supports the evolution of a persistent pregnancy-related health summary record, with information gradually accumulated or updated, throughout the duration of the pregnancy, labour, birth and the immediate postnatal period. As the data is committed to the persistent health record, the date of the update is also recorded in the 'Last Updated' data element in Protocol, to ensure that if this pregnancy summary is taken out of context of the health record for other purposes, such as data exchange, the date of the latest update is kept with the clinical data.\r\n\r\nAfter birth, this summary record can be used to share essential information with other healthcare providers about the pregnancy, labour, birth and immediate postnatal period. \r\n\r\nEach completed pregnancy summary saved to the health record can be re-used to populate the Past Pregnancy History details in subsequent pregnancy records.\r\n\r\nIn situations where completed pregnancy summaries are not available for each previous pregnancy, this archetype can also be used to record a relevant subset of information that can be used to populate the Past Pregnancy History details with new or active pregnancy records. (en)",
          "misuse" : "Não deve ser utilizado para gravar informação baseada em eventos durante a gravidez, parto, nascimento e período pós-natal imediato. Estes serão gravados utilizando arquétipos de OBSERVAÇÃO - por exemplo, a informação relacionada com a história e exame durante consultas pré-natais ou durante o parto.\r\n\r\nNão deve ser usado para gravar resumo de informações sobre a história obstétrica de uma mulher - usar EVALUATION.obstetric_summary.\r\n\r\nNão deve ser usado para gravar informações detalhadas sobre o ciclo menstrual de uma mulher - usar OBSERVATION.menstrual_cycle.\r\n\r\nNão deve ser usado para registrar informações detalhadas sobre a alimentação infantil - um arquétipo separado deverá ser utilizado.\r\n\r\nNão deve ser usado para registrar um resumo ou um diário da história menstrual (geral ou diária) - um arquétipo separado deverá ser utilizado.",
          "copyright" : "© openEHR Foundation",
          "originalResourceUri" : { },
          "otherDetails" : { }
        },
        "en" : {
          "@type" : "RESOURCE_DESCRIPTION_ITEM",
          "language" : {
            "terminologyId" : {
              "value" : "ISO_639-1"
            },
            "codeString" : "en"
          },
          "purpose" : "To support the recording of an overview or summary record of an identified pregnancy and outcome, including the antenatal period, labor, birth and the immediate postnatal period.",
          "keywords" : [ "pregnancy", "fetus", "foetus", "infant", "neonate", "delivery", "conception", "due", "date", "expected", "labor", "labour", "birth", "baby", "babies", "EDD", "EDB" ],
          "use" : "Use to record an overview or summary record of an identified pregnancy and outcome, including the antenatal period, labor, birth and the immediate postnatal period. \r\n\r\nDuring an active pregnancy, this archetype supports the evolution of a persistent pregnancy-related health summary record, with information gradually accumulated or updated, throughout the duration of the pregnancy, labour, birth and the immediate postnatal period. As the data is committed to the persistent health record, the date of the update is also recorded in the 'Last Updated' data element in Protocol, to ensure that if this pregnancy summary is taken out of context of the health record for other purposes, such as data exchange, the date of the latest update is kept with the clinical data.\r\n\r\nAfter birth, this summary record can be used to share essential information with other healthcare providers about the pregnancy, labour, birth and immediate postnatal period. \r\n\r\nEach completed pregnancy summary saved to the health record can be re-used to populate the Past Pregnancy History details in subsequent pregnancy records.\r\n\r\nIn situations where completed pregnancy summaries are not available for each previous pregnancy, this archetype can also be used to record a relevant subset of information that can be used to populate the Past Pregnancy History details with new or active pregnancy records.",
          "misuse" : "Not to be used to record event-based information during the pregnancy, labor, birth and immediate postnatal period. These will be recorded using OBSERVATION archetypes - for example, the information related to history & examination during antenatal visits or during labour.\r\n\r\nNot to be used to record summary information about a woman's Obstetric history - use EVALUATION.obstetric_summary.\r\n\r\nNot to be used to record detailed information about a woman's Menstrual Cycle - use OBSERVATION.menstrual_cycle.\r\n\r\nNot to be used to record detailed information about infant feeding - a separate archetype will be used.\r\n\r\nNot to be used to record a general menstrual history summary or diary - separate archetypes will be used.",
          "copyright" : "© openEHR Foundation",
          "originalResourceUri" : { },
          "otherDetails" : { }
        },
        "ca" : {
          "@type" : "RESOURCE_DESCRIPTION_ITEM",
          "language" : {
            "terminologyId" : {
              "value" : "ISO_639-1"
            },
            "codeString" : "ca"
          },
          "purpose" : "Per donar suport a l'enregistrament d'una visió general o un registre resum d'un determinat embaràs i resultat, inclòs el període prenatal, el treball de part, el naixementi el període postnatal immediat.",
          "keywords" : [ "embaràs", "fetus", "fetus", "infant", "nounat", "deslliurament", "concepció", "previst", "data", "esperat", "treball de part", "part", "naixement", "nadó", "nadons", "DPP" ],
          "use" : "Utilitzeu-lo per registrar una visió general o un registre resum d'un embaràs i resultat identificats, inclosos el període prenatal, el treball de part, el naixement i el període postnatal immediat.\r\n\r\nDurant un embaràs actiu, aquest arquetip dóna suport a l'evolució d'un registre persistent del resum de salut relacionat amb l'embaràs, amb informació acumulada o actualitzada progressivament, al llarg de la durada de l'embaràs, treball de part, part i postnatal immediat. Com que les dades estan compromeses amb la història clínica persistent, la data de l'actualització també es registra a l'element de dades \"Darrera actualització\" del Protocol, per garantir que si aquest resum de l'embaràs es treu fora de context de la història clínica per a altres finalitats, com ara l'intercanvi de dades, la data de l'última actualització es manté amb les dades clíniques.\r\n\r\nDesprés del part, aquest registre resum es pot utilitzar per compartir informació essencial amb altres proveïdors d'atenció mèdica sobre l'embaràs, el treball de part, el part i el període postnatal immediat.\r\n\r\nCada resum de l'embaràs completat desat al registre de salut es pot reutilitzar per omplir els detalls de l'historial d'embaràs anterior als registres d'embaràs posteriors.\r\n\r\nEn situacions en què els resums d'embaràs completats no estan disponibles per a cada embaràs anterior, aquest arquetip també es pot utilitzar per registrar un subconjunt d'informació rellevant que es pot utilitzar per omplir els detalls de l'historial d'embaràs anterior amb registres d'embaràs nous o actius.",
          "misuse" : "No s'ha d'utilitzar per registrar informació basada en esdeveniments durant l'embaràs, el treball de part, el naixement i el període postnatal immediat. Aquests es registraran mitjançant arquetips d'OBSERVATION, per exemple, la informació relacionada amb la història i l'examen durant les visites prenatals o durant el part.\r\n\r\nNo s'ha d'utilitzar per registrar informació resumida sobre la història obstètrica d'una dona - utilitzeu EVALUATION.obstetric_summary.\r\n\r\nNo s'ha d'utilitzar per registrar informació detallada sobre el cicle menstrual d'una dona - utilitzeu OBSERVATION.menstrual_cycle.\r\n\r\nNo s'utilitzarà per registrar informació detallada sobre l'alimentació infantil - s'utilitzarà un arquetip separat.\r\n\r\nNo s'utilitzarà per registrar un resum o un diari general de la història menstrual - s'utilitzaran arquetips separats.",
          "originalResourceUri" : { },
          "otherDetails" : { }
        },
        "es" : {
          "@type" : "RESOURCE_DESCRIPTION_ITEM",
          "language" : {
            "terminologyId" : {
